WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:01.701
-Welcome, welcome, welcome to

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.033
"The Tonight Show"!

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.567
You're here. You made it.

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:05.968
You're watching.
Thank you for tuning in.

00:00:05.968 --> 00:00:07.534
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:07.534 --> 00:00:09.400
Well, guys, today in Washington,

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.100
it was Day 2
of confirmation hearings

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.167
for Supreme Court nominee
Ketanji Brown Jackson.

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:17.300
-Whoo!
-Yep, these hearings are never

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.868
really fun, but then again,

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:20.300
there's always a paper crinkle

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.200
to really liven things up.
Watch this.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.534
Uh, unfortunately,

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:29.067
[ Page turns ]
there's a 77% record --

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:30.367
I'm sorry.
Let me make sure

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:31.634
[ Laughter ]
that this is accurate.

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:34.634
[ Pages turning ]

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:37.634
[ Laughter continues ]

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:42.801
[ Pages turning ]

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:44.701
[ Rubbing microphone ]

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:46.367
United States v Platz.

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:47.400
Trump-appointed

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:48.968
Judge Sarah Pitlyk --
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:48.968 --> 00:00:50.934
[ Laughter ]
Oh, my goodness. Yeah, yeah.

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:53.534
Even old people unwrapping hard
candy at the movies were like,

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:55.567
"Let's go, buddy, come on!"

00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:59.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:01.367
Chomping on gum.
I love it.

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:04.367
Yeah, Judge Jackson spent
all day answering questions.

00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:06.133
Meanwhile, can we see
the Republican senators

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:07.434
who are asking them?

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.534
Gosh, it looks like
the Employee of the Month wall

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:10.534
at Cracker Barrel.

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:12.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.534
But they're really trying
to get people

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:14.701
to watch
the confirmation hearings.

00:01:14.701 --> 00:01:16.334
Check out how they started
the broadcast

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:17.868
on CSPAN.
Look at this.

00:01:17.868 --> 00:01:19.901
-Here we go!

00:01:21.234 --> 00:01:22.200
[ Laughter ]
-[ Clears throat ]

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.968
[ Pages turning ]
-Uh, let's see.

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:25.767
-Ump attack.
-Um...

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:27.400
-This is going to be
a wild ride.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:30.667
-I'm sorry.
-Anything can happen in March!

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:33.567
-Absolute madness!

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:34.801
-Lunch break.
-Yeah.

00:01:34.801 --> 00:01:37.200
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.067
Little cheese break.

00:01:39.067 --> 00:01:40.901
That's right,
today Judge Jackson spent hours

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:41.901
answering questions.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.901
Most Senators didn't get
to be there,

00:01:43.901 --> 00:01:45.501
but here at "The Tonight Show,"
we got ahold

00:01:45.501 --> 00:01:47.033
of the questions
they would've asked.

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:48.367
-Really?
-Yeah, check these out.

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:51.834
First, we have...

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:52.601
They would've asked...

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:57.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:57.634 --> 00:01:58.767
That's a question they had.
-Question.

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:01.701
-Up next we have...

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:02.367
He would've asked...

00:02:04.334 --> 00:02:06.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:06.534 --> 00:02:08.300
Finally, we have...

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:09.033
He would've asked..

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.868
[ Laughter and applause ]
-That's a hard no on that one.

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:14.834
What?

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.167
Some more news --
President Biden just warned

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:20.267
that Russia could be
exploring options

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:23.334
for cyberattacks
against the U.S.

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:25.634
Isn't that always true?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.634 --> 00:02:27.334
It's kind of like saying
Michael Bublé is exploring

00:02:27.334 --> 00:02:29.801
another Christmas album.
It's like, yeah,

00:02:29.801 --> 00:02:31.100
pretty sure it's going
to happen.

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.601 --> 00:02:36.267
Biden said that they could hit
power grids and water supplies.

00:02:36.267 --> 00:02:37.601
And people were like, "Cool,
just let us know

00:02:37.601 --> 00:02:39.133
when TikTok's in danger, okay?"

00:02:39.133 --> 00:02:40.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:41.868
Meanwhile,
to protect yourself online,

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:43.267
experts are saying
that you should make

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:46.267
your passwords longer
than eight characters.

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:47.834
[ Audience murmuring ]
Americans were like, "So,

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:50.701
12345678!"

00:02:50.701 --> 00:02:54.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:56.234
Some business news --
Zoom has introduced

00:02:56.234 --> 00:02:58.200
a new avatar feature
that lets users

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.200
show up to meetings
as an animal,

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:03.000
[ Laughter ]
like a dog, a rabbit, or a fox.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.367
Yeah. There's nothing
like getting laid off

00:03:05.367 --> 00:03:06.934
by a fox in the Bahamas.

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:08.701
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:11.000
Hey, this is cool --
a company claims it invented

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.834
an invisibility shield
that can hide an entire person.

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:15.834
Look at this.

00:03:15.834 --> 00:03:18.934
[ Ethereal tune plays ]

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:19.734
-Mm.

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:23.968
♪♪

00:03:23.968 --> 00:03:24.634
Mm.

00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:29.367
♪♪

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:33.033
[ Laughter ]
Mm.

00:03:33.033 --> 00:03:35.534
Well, congrats, gang, you just
invented the shower door.

00:03:35.534 --> 00:03:38.567
[ Laughter and applause ]
Amazing, really. Wow.

00:03:44.334 --> 00:03:46.567
And, finally, a 101-year-old man

00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:49.234
who dropped out of high school
in the 1930s

00:03:49.234 --> 00:03:52.901
just got his diploma,
more than 80 years later.

00:03:52.901 --> 00:03:56.200
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.400
Asked what he's going to do now,
the guy said,

00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:59.801
"Spring break!"

